🎯 FINAL INTERVIEW ANSWER
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

In microservices, @Transactional works only within a single database and cannot manage
transactions across multiple services. Each service completes its own local transaction
and communicates changes through events.

To maintain business consistency, most organizations use the Saga Pattern with compensation logic.
Reliable event publishing is achieved using the Transactional Outbox Pattern, while Idempotency, 
Retries, and DLQs ensure messages are processed safely and reliably.

The overall objective is to build scalable, fault-tolerant systems that achieve eventual consistency
instead of relying on expensive distributed ACID transactions.
